<title>CANADA: Davis emerges from court protection.</title>
<headline>Davis emerges from court protection.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Davis Distributing Ltd said on Monday it had received court approval for its proposal, which was previously accepted by creditors, and Davis' collector status under the Tobacco Tax Act has been reinstated.</p>
<p>Davis had filed for creditor protection on May 22, 1996.</p>
<p>Company president Bernard Davis said Davis Distributing has concentrated effectively on achieving a scale of operations and range of distribution services that &quot;should permit efficient and profitable operations as 1997 progresses.&quot;</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
